    "created_at": "2023-03-31T22:11:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-31T22:11:38Z",
    "body": "> Another point that was brought up is that we should revisit whether `autocomplete=no` is really in the interests of end users.\r\n\r\nI'm ok considering whether `autocomplete` should control form restoration, but if the answer is \"no\", then there definitely needs to be a replacement attribute that *can* control form restoration. E.g. `formstaterestoration=off` or something. This is a real use case, in production on several big sites.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
