    "updated_at": "2023-05-26T19:33:30Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the detailed analysis! It feels like we shouldn't require JS to implement this behavior, since an attribute feels the most natural. It's quite frustrating to developers to need to do tricks to get browsers to do what they want, such as `autocomplete=nope`. If we don't want `autocomplete` to be the knob used to control form restoration, then we should provide another (attribute) knob, in my opinion.\r\n\r\nQuick side note about `textarea` - I changed Chromium to not restore `<textarea autocomplete=off>` in [February](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/4288939).",
